  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-based Initiative for Integrated Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project Community-based Initiative for Integrated Education will be implemented in 10 communities across Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH) focusing on ethnically-challenged Herzegovina-Neretva and Central-Bosnia Cantons and predominantly mono-ethnic communities in the entity Republika Srpska. These communities are: Stolac, Prozor-Rama, Ljubinje, Nevesinje, Capljina, Citluk, Konjic, Gornji Vakuf-Uskoplje, Bugojno and Mostar.</narrative>
  </description>
